@startuml alert-delivery
title US-03: Alert Delivery - Final v1 delivery path

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Kafka
participant "API\n(consuming instance)" as APIConsumer
database "TimescaleDB\nalerts" as TSDB
database "Redis\nalert-events\n(pub/sub)" as RedisPubSub
participant "API\n(all instances)" as APIAll
participant "Angular\nDashboard" as Dashboard
actor Operator

note over APIConsumer, APIAll
  This diagram shows final v1 delivery.
  Phase 03 proves one API instance + authenticated WebSocket.
  Phase 07 adds workspace scope.
  Phase 08 adds cross-instance Redis fan-out.
end note

Kafka -> APIConsumer : consume SIGNAL_LOSS\n{ alert_id, entity_id, alert_type, payload... }
APIConsumer -> TSDB : INSERT alert\nON CONFLICT (alert_id) DO NOTHING
TSDB --> APIConsumer : inserted or replay no-op

APIConsumer -> RedisPubSub : PUBLISH ALERT_CREATED\n{ alert_id, ... }
RedisPubSub --> APIAll : broadcast to subscribers
APIAll --> Dashboard : push WebSocket event\nwhen connection scope matches
Dashboard --> Operator : display SIGNAL_LOSS

note over APIConsumer
  Commit ordering:
  1. durable DB write
  2. Redis publish
  3. Kafka offset commit

  Crash/replay can repeat WebSocket delivery.
  Durable row remains duplicate-free.
end note

note over Dashboard
  Deduplicate repeated alert events by alert_id.
  Transport is at-least-once, not exactly-once.
end note

@enduml
